    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Hey I don't think it's a good idea to remap `-` to opening parent directories (#40426). I use `<CR>` and `-` in normal mode at least as much as I use `j` and `k`, but now `-` is gone. It's like if you remapped normal-mode `h` to opening help or something. Vanilla Neovim is unusable for me now: the damn directory listing keeps opening itself when I'm just trying to move the cursor around a file. The silver lining is that `-u NONE` doesn't load the default mappings, so when SSHing into servers there's still an escape hatch.\n\nPlease consider remapping an unused key sequence instead, like `'-`. Or maybe `q-`, in the spirit of `q:`, though it wouldn't work in macros. Or, now that `gr` is gone, perhaps `gr-`?",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
